Cap the pointer range so its metadata fits

The pointer range is half of the free kernel VA, and with 4 KiB pages every 128 KiB
of it needs a kmem_page_meta entry.  The metadata claim cannot cover that, so
kmem_get_new_chunk() finds the high watermarks met and returns NULL forever, which
is the spin at kmem_locate_space.  Cap the pointer range at 64 GiB.
---
diff --git a/osfmk/vm/vm_kern.c b/osfmk/vm/vm_kern.c
index 2927d4b..c3289dd 100644
--- a/osfmk/vm/vm_kern.c
+++ b/osfmk/vm/vm_kern.c
@@ -3501,6 +3501,15 @@ kmem_add_extra_claims(void)
 	 * ranges divide the available VA by 8.
 	 */
 	ptr_range_size = largest_free_size / ((kmem_ptr_ranges + 1) * 2);
+	/*
+	 * nio: this divides the whole free kernel VA, which with 4 KiB pages needs
+	 * one kmem_page_meta per 128 KiB of pointer range and cannot be mapped, so
+	 * the very first chunk request runs out of meta and spins.  Sixty-four
+	 * gigabytes of pointer VA is far more than an eight gigabyte board uses.
+	 */
+	if (ptr_range_size > (vm_map_size_t)64 * 1024 * 1024 * 1024) {
+		ptr_range_size = (vm_map_size_t)64 * 1024 * 1024 * 1024;
+	}
 	sprayqtn_range_size = ptr_range_size;
 
 	if (sprayqtn_range_size > (sane_size / 2)) {
